\subsection{Definitions and mathematical statement}
\paragraph{Statement recorded in the supplied source.}
Must a complex domain diffeomorphic to $R^{2m}$, $m\geq 2$, carrying a complete smooth Kähler metric with $sec\leq -1$ possess a nonconstant bounded holomorphic function? No finite lower bound on sectional curvature is imposed.

\subsection{Short English statement}
Must a complex domain diffeomorphic to $R^{2m}$, $m\geq 2$, carrying a complete smooth Kähler metric with $sec\leq -1$ possess a nonconstant bounded holomorphic function? No finite lower bound on sectional curvature is imposed.

